y continues d4 (40%), Nf3 (31%), Bc4 (11%). Your pawn is the one to watch (often landing on c5, e6). Aim at their knight.","tips":["Aim for a steady edge by move 15: 54% of games get there, and 36% reach +6 by move 21.","Watch your bishop: it is behind 19% of your lost leads, 1.2\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the light-squared bishop (57%), landing on d6, d5, b7.","Aim at their bishop: it is behind 20% of their lost leads, 1.2\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the dark-squared bishop (50%). The reply wins it outright 24% of the time. Take it with a pawn.","Material changes hands for you on e4 and f3: build pressure there.","They win material on a6 and f6: keep those squares defended.","Look for the pin: it appears 1.9\u00d7 as often as usual in this opening."],"similar":[],"family":"Ware Defense","children":[]}